`@objectstack/plugin-dev#test` failing on main with 2 test failures: metadata stub async/sync mismatch and CI timeout.

- **Metadata stub methods made synchronous** — `createMetadataStub()` methods were `async`, so `Array.isArray(metadata.list('object'))` evaluated `Array.isArray(Promise)` → `false`. Removed `async` since these are simple Map operations; `await` on sync return values is still safe for callers.

- **`register()` signature fixed** — stub expected `(type, name, data)` but test calls `register('object', { name: 'account' })`. Now accepts both forms, extracting name from `definition.name` when second arg is an object:
  ```ts
  register(type: string, nameOrDef: string | Record<string, any>, data?: unknown) {
    if (typeof nameOrDef === 'object' && nameOrDef !== null) {
      const key = nameOrDef.name ?? nameOrDef.id ?? 'unknown';
      store.get(type)!.set(key, nameOrDef);
    } else {
      store.get(type)!.set(nameOrDef, data);
    }
  }
  ```

- **Init test timeout increased** — dynamic imports of real peer-dep plugins are slow in CI; bumped from default 5s to 15s.

